    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d888">

                <pb facs="0762" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/313</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Messersmith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 137</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-02">July 2, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your
                    despatch no. 467 of June 24, 1940<anchor n="30" xml:id="d888-f1"/> with regard
                    to President Laredo Brú’s message to the Cuban Congress urging the settlement of
                    “the rest of the obligations originating in the public works program”.</p>
                <p>You are authorized in your discretion to state to the appropriate officials of
                    the Cuban Government that the Department hopes that this matter will be settled
                    on the basis of the agreement reached between the Cuban Government and the
                    creditors in November 1938,<anchor n="31" xml:id="d888-f2"/> which agreement was
                    incorporated in a bill introduced into the Cuban Senate by Senator Casanova in
                    the same month. You will wish to stress the fact that the debt owed to the firm
                    of Purdy and Henderson was included in this settlement. It is the Department’s
                    view that the agreement in question now constitutes a clearly recognized
                    obligation of the Cuban Government to the creditors in question and that <pb
                        facs="0763" n="751" xml:id="pg751"/> there would be no justification for any
                    further investigation or review of the claims.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
